  "description": "MedEmbed Small is an Apache-2.0 sentence-transformers embedding model fine-tuned from BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5 for medical and clinical information retrieval. The established hidden TEI CUDA 1.9.3 Forge row supports B200, H200, L40S, and RTX6000 but failed at B300 pod startup; the same TEI CUDA 1.9.3 digest independently logged `cuda compute cap 103 is not supported` for the PubMedBERT TEI B300 diagnostic. This separate hidden manifest adds a B300 fallback without changing the TEI row: reuse the already mirrored official vLLM 0.21.0 CUDA 13 image, launch it with `--runner pooling`, and select CLS pooling with pooler activation enabled so vLLM applies the normalization required by MedEmbed's sentence-transformers `2_Normalize` module. The Hugging Face API recheck on 2026-05-27T21Z reported the artifact public, ungated, enabled, Apache-2.0 licensed, sentence-transformers based, revision 40a5850d046cfdb56154e332b4d7099b63e8d50e, and safetensors-backed with 33,360,000 F32 parameters. The 2026-05-27T19Z B300/uk-south1 hidden probe succeeded with 3 warmups and 10 measured requests; the 2026-05-27T20Z parity pass found the old no-activation profile directionally equivalent but unnormalized, so this manifest enables activation. The corrected 2026-05-27T20Z B300 smoke succeeded, and the normalized-output check over eight synthetic non-PHI HCLS texts produced unit-norm vLLM embeddings with max first-eight-dimension delta 0.00021141 versus TEI. The 2026-05-27T21Z normalized B300 probe then succeeded with 3 warmups, 10 measured requests, 53.467 s startup, 70 ms client-wall median request time, 871.43 tokens/s, and 0.98 GB VRAM. The 2026-05-27T22Z gate adds research-only acknowledgement metadata and confirms the public catalog route remains hidden with HTTP 404. Keep this row hidden/onboarding/default-ineligible until healthcare product safety review approves publication and product chooses the MedEmbed family routing plan.",
